==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|colloïde}}, from {{uder|en|grc|κόλλα||glue}} + {{m|en|-oid}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɒlɔɪd/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[glue|Glue]]-like; [[gelatinous]].
#: '''''colloid''' tumours''

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chemistry}} A [[stable]] system of two [[phase]]s, one of which is [[dispersed]] in the other in the form of very small [[droplet]]s or [[particle]]s.
# {{lb|en|meteorology}} An [[intimate]] [[mixture]] of two [[substances]], one of which, called the [[dispersed]] phase (or '''colloid'''), is uniformly distributed in a finely divided state throughout the second substance, called the [[dispersion]] medium (or dispersing medium).
# {{lb|en|geology}} A [[particle]] less than 1 [[micron]] in [[diameter]], following the [[Wentworth scale]]

